IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il48-nouns`
IMPORT `il48-cross-references`

-- Row il-48. The sound citations point at what their citing words say, the printed figure agrees, and the recorded facts about the two defects and the controls are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: their four failing assertions are in il48-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in il48-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the sound citations`

-- The two controls point at what they say.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ב)(3), a fixed addition`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 14א(א) to s 6א(א)(1) to (3), the three conditions`)

§ `Tests of the printed figure`

-- The divisor in the deposited consolidation is the one the official instrument prints.
#ASSERT `the deposited figure is the one the official instrument prints` (`printed figure: the number in the definition of the hourly minimum wage`)
#ASSERT (`printed figure: the number in the definition of the hourly minimum wage`)'s `the official instrument prints` EQUALS 186
#ASSERT (`printed figure: the number in the definition of the hourly minimum wage`)'s `the deposited consolidation prints` EQUALS 186
#ASSERT (`printed figure: the number in the definition of the hourly minimum wage`)'s `the official figure was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- No citation here has both limbs read from the official instruments alone: each has a limb that is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY, either the whole limb or that no later instrument touched the words.
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ב)(3), a fixed addition`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: definition of the average wage to NII 1968 s 1`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 14א(א) to s 6א(א)(1) to (3), the three conditions`))
-- The first defect: limb (a), the repeal, is read from the page image; limb (b) is read from the page images with the caveat.
#ASSERT (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
-- Its control: both limbs carry the caveat.
#ASSERT (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ב)(3), a fixed addition`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ב)(3), a fixed addition`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
-- The second defect: limb (a), the replacement of the 1968 version, is the consolidation only; limb (b) carries the caveat.
#ASSERT (`reference: definition of the average wage to NII 1968 s 1`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: definition of the average wage to NII 1968 s 1`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
-- The second control: both limbs are the consolidation only.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 14א(א) to s 6א(א)(1) to (3), the three conditions`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 14א(א) to s 6א(א)(1) to (3), the three conditions`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`

§ `Tests of what the two descriptions of the defects say`

-- What the citing words say it points at, and what the target is, as the texts show them.
#ASSERT (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `section 3(ג) of the Law as made: the rule on counting a premium as a pay component`
#ASSERT (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a subsection of the Law that was repealed, so that the section prints no text for it`
#ASSERT (`reference: definition of the average wage to NII 1968 s 1`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `the definition of the average wage in section 1 of the National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], 5728-1968`
#ASSERT (`reference: definition of the average wage to NII 1968 s 1`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `the definition of the average wage in section 1 of the National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], 5755-1995`

§ `Tests of the day the named text stopped being in force`

-- Sefer HaChukim 1621 p. 129, section 12: the repeal of section 3(ג) commences on 23 Adar II 5757 = 1 April 1997.
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`) (Date 1 4 1997) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`) (Date 2 4 1997) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The day before: no source held says whether it was amended between 1987 and 1997, so NOTHING (fork D1 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`) (Date 31 3 1997) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`) (Date 9 4 1987) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The 1968 version: replaced from 7 Tishrei 5756 = 1 October 1995 (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY).
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: definition of the average wage to NII 1968 s 1`) (Date 1 10 1995) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: definition of the average wage to NII 1968 s 1`) (Date 30 9 1995) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A control has no recorded end: NOTHING on any day, which is not a statement that the target stands.
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ב)(3), a fixed addition`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: s 14א(א) to s 6א(א)(1) to (3), the three conditions`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests of the documented fork of the Interpretation Law section 25`

-- Reading A of the second defect: read through section 25, the citing words reach the 1995 definition, which is the target. The row records the reading and does not rule on it (fork P2 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the citation reaches its target once read through the Interpretation Law section 25` (`reference: definition of the average wage to NII 1968 s 1`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The row does not say what section 25 does for the other references: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the citation reaches its target once read through the Interpretation Law section 25` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the citation reaches its target once read through the Interpretation Law section 25` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ב)(3), a fixed addition`) EQUALS NOTHING
